{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-L14-watch-app-01","date":"2026-11-21","lens":"14","surface":"watch","area":"watch/app","refs":["F-watch-102","F-watch-103","F-watch-106","F-watch-109","F-watch-115","F-watch-116"],"severity":"S3","title":"When the watch app fails or crashes on a member's wrist, MettleUp never hears of it","what":"The watch app has no crash report of its own and no internet access. Every failure it catches (a set not sent to the phone, the phone refusing a set, a phone message it could not read, a rest card button that did nothing) is written only to the watch's own log, which nobody at MettleUp can see. The only thing that ever reaches MettleUp is the screen diary, and only when the member ticks 'Add my watch's screen log' in the phone's Help and feedback, and that diary holds screen and battery events, not these failures. So a watch model where logging from the watch keeps failing, or where the app crashes, stays invisible unless a member writes in.","expected":"The watch keeps a short list of its own failures and crashes and passes it to the phone, which sends it with the phone's crash reports; the owner sees watch problems in the same place as phone problems.","evidence":["apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:10-31","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchActions.kt:55-56","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchActions.kt:103-104","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchActions.kt:122","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchSync.kt:58-59","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/DiagSend.kt:9-14"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"watch-failures-never-reach-owner","who":"members with a watch, and the owner","how_often":"every time the watch fails","fix_line":"Have the watch hand its failures and crashes to the phone so they go out with the phone's crash reports","fix_size":"medium","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
